# PLACEHOLDER — the serverless-GPU model-server image (decision **D15**). A10 builds it.
#
# This file documents the contract so the CPU worker's `ServerlessWhisperProvider`
# and the Terraform in `infra/` can be written against something concrete. It is
# deliberately not built by CI: nothing in Wave 1 needs a GPU, and a CUDA base
# layer is ~4 GB.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What runs in it (D15, `09 §9`)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One model server, co-hosting the three models that all need the same GPU so a
# transcript never crosses an instance boundary mid-file:
#
#   * faster-whisper `large-v3-turbo`  (float16, CTranslate2)
#   * the forced aligners of `09 §2`   (IndicWav2Vec CTC MIT, XLSR-53 Apache-2.0;
#                                       Meta MMS is excluded, CC-BY-NC-4.0, D77)
#   * pyannote community-1 diarisation (CC-BY-4.0 — attribution required)
#
# Weights are baked into the image, never downloaded at boot: a per-second
# serverless instance that spends 40 s pulling from Hugging Face has already lost
# the latency budget of `09 §9` (ASR ≤ 30 s for a 5-minute clip).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The HTTP contract `providers/serverless_whisper.py` speaks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   POST /transcribe
#   Authorization: Bearer {GPU_PROVIDER_TOKEN}
#   { "audio": "<https url or base64 wav>", "language": "hi",
#     "wordTimestamps": true, "hints": ["..."], "model": "large-v3-turbo" }
#
#   200 { "language": "hi", "languageProbability": 0.98, "durationS": 41.2,
#         "model": "large-v3-turbo", "requestId": "...",
#         "words": [{ "start": 0.12, "end": 0.44, "word": "toh", "probability": 0.94 }],
#         "segments": [{ "start": 0.0, "end": 4.1, "text": "..." }] }
#
# Times on the wire are **seconds**; the adapter converts to integer milliseconds.
# `GET /health` must answer without touching a model, so a cold instance is
# reported ready only once the weights are resident.
#
# Retention: the instance holds audio for the duration of the request and nothing
# is written to disk, which is the `retentionClass: ephemeral` the adapter records
# in `provider_submissions`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sketch (A10 completes and pins every version)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FROM nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu22.04
#
# RUN apt-get update && apt-get install --no-install-recommends -y \
#         python3.12 python3-pip ffmpeg ca-certificates \
#     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
#
# COPY requirements-gpu.lock ./
# RUN python3.12 -m pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements-gpu.lock
#
# # Bake the weights. Each RUN is its own layer so a model change does not
# # invalidate the others.
# RUN python3.12 -c "from faster_whisper import WhisperModel; \
#       WhisperModel('large-v3-turbo', device='cuda', compute_type='float16')"
# RUN python3.12 -c "import pyannote.audio  # community-1, CC-BY-4.0"
#
# ENV MODEL_NAME=large-v3-turbo COMPUTE_TYPE=float16 WARM_FLOOR=1
# EXPOSE 8000
# CMD ["python3.12", "-m", "gpu_server"]
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operational notes for A10
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * Warm floor of one instance per region (D15); scale to zero everywhere else.
# * Reserved L4/L40S only above ~150 000 media-minutes per month, after measuring
#   real L4 RTF — not before.
# * The image is the unit of rollback: pin it by digest in the Helm values so a
#   model regression is one value change.
